WEBVTT

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.740
<b>I Love You</b>

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.740
<b>I Love You</b>

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:10.870
Bisco!

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.690
Whoa, hey, don't get up. I just 
finished wrapping those bandages.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.150
Bisco?

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.810
Where...

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:20.860
Are you there?

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.410
My eyes... I...

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.790
Don't worry.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.590
I'm right here.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.920
Don't start trembling over that, dummy.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.060
You'll be better once the medicine kicks in.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.140
Medicine? An injection?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.940
I stole some Rust Eater 
from Kurokawa's place.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.970
You mixed it yourself?

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.400
Those instructions you wrote
down were really useful.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.700
You usually don't study 
my notes at all, though.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.100
Keep complaining and I'll toss it.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.300
Don't move.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.750
Wait, what about you?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.270
No, stop. You need it first.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:10.800
I already injected myself with some.
 You don't need to worry.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.420
Really?

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.630
You planning to keep your 
hand there until morning?

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.780
I'm injecting you now.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.890
Are you angry?

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:37.120
Because I played by my own rules,
and made you lose like that...

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.680
Nah, I'm not angry.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.500
You're not?

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.300
If our positions had been reversed, 
I'd have done the same.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:49.740
We're both still alive, 
so it was a draw. I didn't lose.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.360
I wonder what happened to Jabi-san.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.690
That old man's got the devil's luck.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.040
He probably got away.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.720
He said he rescued Pawoo.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.260
Yeah.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.920
Your older sister's an 
impressive woman, too.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.550
As long as she's got her pole, 
she won't get captured.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.300
I see.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.870
Hey, Bisco...

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.930
Wanna go out with Pawoo?

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.120
Huh?!

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.950
If you gave her a little push now, I bet she'd 
fall for you. She seems to like you, too.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:29.040
D-Don't be stupid! The woman who 
came at me swinging an iron pole?!

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.740
She's the most beautiful woman
 in Imihama, and on top of that...

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.820
Check this out.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.200
She's an E-cup!

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.810
It's probably all muscle.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.590
No Kishimojin for me.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.930
She's pretty sensitive, you know.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.870
Though, given how little experience you've 
had with women, you might not understand.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:51.820
Oh? You make it sound like you've had plenty.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:52.880
Because I have?

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.530
But I don't think Pawoo's all
 that experienced, either.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.660
With her personality, 
her love can be... kinda heavy.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.660
Her last boyfriend...

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:04.020
Cheated on her and died by her hand?

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.380
Of course not.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.580
I did the surgery on him.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.190
That's not funny at all.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.210
You wouldn't cheat on her, 
so she wouldn't beat you.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:18.130
Try having this same conversation with
 your sister. She'd send you flying.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.220
I had a dream just now.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:31.340
We were all traveling together
and found a good plot of land.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:35.280
We lived there for a while, and when we 
got tired of the place, we set out again.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.960
I bet that'd be wonderful.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.200
But... you're going, aren't you?

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.170
You're going to settle things 
with Kurokawa, right?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.070
Yeah. I am.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.500
I'll get stronger. Much stronger.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.510
Strong enough for you to 
trust me to cover your back.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:04.440
You're strong enough already.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.310
We're partners, right?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.090
Together, we can go anywhere.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.180
We can beat anything.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:13.940
That's right.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.430
Partners stick together forever, right?

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:17.930
That's right.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.450
Even when they die?

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.570
That's right.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.530
Hey, Bisco, are you there?

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.360
I'm right beside you.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.930
Would you... hold my hand?

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:35.640
Sure.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.690
Are you there?

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:40.830
I'm here.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:43.730
Sleep.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:48.340
Your body's had all it can handle. 
Sleep is what you need right now.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:50.390
Don't leave me, Bisco.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.120
I'm not going anywhere.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:58.200
You'll be here... when I wake up?

00:06:58.880 --> 00:06:59.970
I will.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:15.880
Now I understand how Jabi 
felt when he was raising me.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:22.300
I was like a firework, expected to just
 burn up and die like a stray dog.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:26.120
Yet you breathed meaning into my life.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:30.210
I helped you grow and protected you.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:34.330
That alone has given my life meaning.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:39.390
Milo, I won't die in despair or carnage.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:43.710
I'll meet my end with dreams of your future.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.440
That's real happiness.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.910
It's more than I deserve.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.240
This is farewell.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:04.560
Y'know, I've never felt so 
calm about risking my life.

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.000
Actagawa.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:10.570
I made a friend.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.960
A real friend.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:23.350
<b>Japanese Government Forces Miyagi Base</b>

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:24.730
<b>Japanese Government Forces Miyagi Base</b>

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.070
<b>Imi</b>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.160
Kurokawa's special forces?

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.080
In government forces trucks?

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.350
Why?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.580
<b>Japanese Government Forces</b>

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.580
<b>Miyagi Base</b>

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.370
<i>What is that?</i>

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:56.460
Hey, aren't you curious?

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:00.990
About why I'm not killing you, I mean.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:03.590
Because it's Respect for the Aged Day?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:08.540
If it was that, I'd have to kill you tomorrow.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:11.410
Well, it'll be faster to just show you.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:18.210
Thanks to the Rust treatments we obtained 
from persecuting Mushroom Keepers,

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:21.660
there are, in fact, fewer
patients with Rusting.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:27.600
Problem is, that upsets the balance 
between supply and demand, you see?

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.860
If there's an abundance of medicine,

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.900
we just need to increase the
 number of patients, right?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.250
No...

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:36.760
This is...

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.890
I'm boiling down the Rust.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.880
You know, the thing about the 
naturally occurring Rust Wind...

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.470
Well, it's hardly had any 
effect for a good while now.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.850
So what are we to do, Jabi?

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:56.420
How did Toyotomi Hideyoshi put it 
again? If the cuckoo doesn't sing...

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.370
You're telling me you're 
artificially creating the Rust Wind?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.160
How on earth...

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:05.770
That's a nice tone I hear in your voice, old man.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:11.100
Long ago, there was a giant 
weapon that covered Japan in Rust

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.190
and contained a Rust 
reactor within its body.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:18.670
It was able to generate an unlimited 
amount of Rust within itself.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.500
And that's it.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:25.350
What you see down there is the 
thing that created the Tokyo crater

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.550
and plunged Japan into a sea of Rust.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.120
Tetsujin!

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:41.090
In Japan, there are five of them...
though some theories state six.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:44.710
This one, however, is one of the
 few Tetsujin that's still functional.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:50.010
Oh, dear. Maybe this is all a bit
 too stimulating for an old-timer?

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:54.030
It's not like I'm trying to 
make Tetsujin operational.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:56.200
Hey, moron, you brewed this too strong.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:01.260
The reactor is functional, though. I can turn
 the concentrated Rust into Rust Bullets

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.520
and fire them out of that 
Ganesha Cannon nearby.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.270
Kaboom!

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:10.020
And then the Rust Wind blows again.

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:17.260
For now, it seems... Weeping Child Ravine,
 was it? That place needs one fired at it.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:21.030
Gotta exterminate the Pipe Snake 
that the Rust Eater grows on.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.090
You wouldn't!

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:26.020
Don't you find that horrifying?
 It goes against all ethics.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:31.790
If I cared about that, I wouldn't have 
betrayed you all in the first place.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.510
You fiend.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.600
Join me, Jabi.

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.380
From what Doctor Panda says,

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:45.040
the Rust Eater requires Mushroom Keeper
 blood to activate its true effects.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:51.070
Would you handpick some young, fresh 
Mushroom Keepers and provide them to me?

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:55.170
It'd be easy for you to 
convince them as their leader.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:12:00.510
Just give one good speech about how 
their noble sacrifice will save the clan.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.700
I'd pay you, of course.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.700
You think I'd ever accept your offer?

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.860
Wrong answer! You have no
 choice but to accept, Jabi.

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:16.170
I just told you, didn't I? I can turn 
anywhere in Japan into a sea of Rust.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:19.700
I could even fire a shot into your
 village of Mushroom Keepers

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.730
before firing at Weeping Child Ravine.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.280
You're able to say it, aren't you, old man?

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:29.220
It just takes one word: "Yes."

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:30.640
Kurokawa.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.320
Hm? What is it?

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:38.930
Idiot.

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:40.850
Just shoot if you're gonna shoot, fool.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.600
You can't shoot it.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.870
Threatening a lone old man is all you 
can do with your tiny speck of courage.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.800
You old bastard!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.120
Hey, idiot. That's enough. Stop.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.120
I can't have him dying on me.

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:06.240
Make sure he can't draw a bow again.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.200
Jabi.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.990
You Mushroom Keepers are famous 
for your cherished bow fingers.

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:16.770
It'd be a shame to lose them, right?

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:20.950
Just say "yes" and your fingers
 are safe. I'll count to ten.

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.100
Ten, nine...

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.620
Do it, Kurokawa.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:30.270
Go ahead and cut an old man's fingers off 
so you can sleep well for just one night.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.780
Zero.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.450
Akaboshi!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:00.510
Tenacious bastard.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.990
Sorry for hitting you, old man.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:04.890
But...

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:08.760
You hit me plenty when I was a kid, 
so we'll call it even, yeah?

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.580
You can't. Not...

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:14.790
Not in that state...

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.600
I'm gonna take Kurokawa down.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:21.950
In the meantime, Jabi, you go 
destroy that Ganesha Cannon thing.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:25.280
That'll save both our 
village and the Rust Eater.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.350
Don't be a fool! And leave you behind?

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.590
You know who I am, old man?

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.360
I'm Bisco.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:37.430
I'm the man you poured 
everything into raising.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:38.590
Have faith in me.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:42.110
Just like I have faith in you.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:47.190
Do you resent me, Bisco?

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.740
Now go, old man.

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.080
Don't die, Bisco.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.930
Bring the you-know-what.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.150
Huh? But it's still not...

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:18.890
Drag that failure out here!

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:19.670
Yes, sir!

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.670
Hey, now...

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.380
I'm at least risking my life over here.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:35.020
If you're gonna be an evil boss,
 you gotta stand proud.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:38.340
Otherwise, you're a buzzkill.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:41.580
Go ahead and write your will
so I can edit it later.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:44.580
Either way, you're dying here!

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:46.650
That right?

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:48.340
So...

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.990
Are you terrified of this half-dead
 piece of scrap, Kurokawa?

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.730
Your knees are trembling!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:01.470
I'll rip your limbs off 
and kill you, Akaboshi!

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.550
Not good.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.100
What is this thing?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.750
<b>Imi</b>

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:29.750
What a rude gorilla. No discipline at all.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:32.250
What monstrous strength.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:32.510
<b>Imi</b>

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:32.590
<b>Imi</b>

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:32.670
<b>Imi</b>

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:32.760
<b>Imi</b>

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.640
<b>Imi</b>

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.630
I'm here to repay last night's favor.

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.810
Akaboshi!

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.870
I-I got him!

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:48.600
I got his eye!

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.950
That guy's your meal today!
 Turn him into paste!

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:38.150
All right!

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:06.430
Your fingers shattered, huh?
 You can't draw your bow now?

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:10.050
This is how it always goes, Akaboshi!

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:14.200
No matter how strong you are, 
I'll win at the last second!

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.210
That's just how this world works.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:23.140
It always makes sure punks like 
you rot to death in the end!

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:32.870
Now why would not being able to 
draw my bow mean you win, Kurokawa?

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:36.170
Go ahead and run, Kurokawa!

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:39.390
As long as I have a single tooth
 or even a single nail left,

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.820
I can kill you at any time!

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:17.800
Stay back!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.750
Stay back, Akaboshi!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:22.150
Die! Just die over there!

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.940
Go to hell,

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.450
Kurokawa!

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:57.080
Wh-What's with that look, Akaboshi?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:00.090
How can you make that face?

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.240
You...

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.040
You were supposed to beat me.

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:11.230
I'll listen to your final request.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.530
Tell me before you die.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.740
No, you tell me yours, idiot.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:20.490
Go die in some worthless 
back alley, Akaboshi.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.320
Kurokawa!

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:32.570
God damn brat!

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.330
Bisco!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.890
So you get to die like in 
one of those movies, huh?

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:51.360
Why don't you try saying, 
"I'll be back," Kurokawa?

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:55.990
Akaboshi! Akaboshi!

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:57.610
I will kill you!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:02.280
I'll kill all the Mushroom 
Keepers, and you, too!

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.610
Then I'll sleep as much as I want!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:09.070
Sleep easy in this sea of Rust you made.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:16.380
Bisco!

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:20.380
You promised me...

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:22.460
You said we were partners.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:25.850
You said we'd be together forever!

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:28.080
No...

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.660
I'll be lonely, Bisco.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:32.270
Don't leave me behind.

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:33.500
Milo.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:39.200
So what if my flesh and bones are gone?

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.190
My soul will never die.

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:45.680
I'll crawl up out of the 
depths of Hell to protect you.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:47.760
Milo.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:49.390
We're partners.

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.270
We'll be together forever.

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:52.530
So...

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:54.810
So smile.

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:59.560
Whenever you're scared or in pain...
At times like that, you have to smile.

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:02.210
Just like I always did.

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:05.710
Whenever you smile, I'll be there, too.

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:14.300
Milo, take my life.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.650
Don't let the Rust kill me.

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:23.070
I want you to put me down and
 take it. Take my life with you.

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:24.700
Can you do it?

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:27.340
Yeah.

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:32.970
I'll try...

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:35.570
I'll try to live like you.

00:22:36.260 --> 00:22:38.530
No matter how often I'm battered or broken,

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:40.570
I'll rise up and smile.

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:42.430
I'll try to live like that.

00:22:43.820 --> 00:22:47.050
And if I give it my all, then one day,

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:51.920
when I'm ripped to pieces, ground 
into dust, and reduced to just a soul,

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:54.970
will I be able to see you again?

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:58.220
Yeah. We'll meet again.

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.490
I love you.

00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:20.690
Even after you're gone, I'll always...

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:24.340
love you.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:37.470
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:37.470
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:28.720
One star shatters and falls,
 leaving an empty void in the sky.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:30.600
Is that red light lost forever?

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:31.450
No!

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:35.570
The sun's arrows pierce our hearts 
and continue to burn red!

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:37.470
Next episode: "Tetsujin Revived."

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.810
God of mushrooms, behold!

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Tetsujin Revived</b>
